// ProjectDeliveryS709 — Sprint 709: Resolve issue542 through dcCiNextestExcludesEveryCustomHarness: CI concluded failure at 1e2ed25 and again at 593147c because ci.yml and release.yml mirror the nextest / cargo-test split by hand from keel-cli's manifest alone, and keel-parser declares four more harness = false cucumber binaries (lexer_bdd, parser_bdd, semantic_bdd, spec_compat_bdd) that cargo nextest run --workspace tries to --list and cannot (exit 104 before one test runs). sprint707's retro looked at exactly this drift and dismissed it. The pain: main is red for two commits on a cause no local check could see - keel suite --touched is scoped to -p keel-cli and never meets those binaries. The fix is the split naming all seven; the control is a guard that derives the expected split from every workspace member's manifest and reads both workflows at every gate, so a new cucumber binary in any crate fails on this machine before it fails on ubuntu. Chartered by D0475 (process-change, accepted by the human 2026-09-14), whose runner this is. 2 pts.. EXECUTE. 2 pts.
